:PNLGRP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP NAME='QRYJOBLOG'.Querry Job Log - Help
:P.
The Querry Job Log (QRYJOBLOG) command builds a temporary file for all job logs
for active jobs for a workstation id, and then runs a query over the file.
:P.
This is inteneded to be used to look for errors in a user job log when they
are running multiple group jobs under one workstation id.
:P.
To use the command just enter it on a command line like this: QRYJOGLOG WS24,
replace WS24 with the correct workstation Id. It opens the SQL command with a
default query statement already entered for the temporary file. Change the
querry to show what you want and press enter to run it.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP NAME='QRYJOBLOG/WRKSTN'.Workstation Id (WRKSTN) - Help
:XH3.Workstation ID (WRKSTN)
:P.
Specifies the workstation to query the job logs for.
:P.
This is a required parameter.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:EPNLGRP.
